{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a visible light-mediated iridium-photocatalyzed reverse polarity Povarov reaction between aryl imines and electron-deficient alkenes. The reaction proceeds via a nucleophilic alpha-amino radical generated by proton-coupled electron transfer (PCET), yielding substituted tetrahydroquinolines with high trans-diastereoselectivity. A key finding is the use of sub-stoichiometric Hantzsch ester (10 mol%) as a reductive initiator for a radical chain process.",
